const T1 = "Wildlife Network shows where birds, bats and other animals are right now, from thousands of community stations and observers. Each dot is a recent detection: blue from BirdWeather stations, amber from GBIF, green from iNaturalist, pink from devices sending directly.";
const T2 = "Type a name to see where it is being heard and seen, how its range centre is shifting, and when it arrives in each region, with the uncertainty of each estimate.";
const T3 = "Switch the animal class. Every measure is worked out per class, so a sparse group is not drowned out by birds.";
const T4 = "Now shows what is changing: species moving, surging or fading, and the latest arrivals. Feed lists the newest detections.";
const T4A = " Ask answers questions in plain words from the same data.";
const T4B = " About has the sources, credits and privacy notes.";
const T5 = "Play the last hours of detections, or pick a species and play a whole year of its movement, week by week.";
const T6 = "A BirdNET-Pi, BirdNET-Go, camera trap, bat detector or a Wildlife Network Base can send its detections here. Everything is open: the methods, the data downloads and the API.";
const AL1 = "One email when it arrives in your area after weeks away, never more than once every two months. Confirm by email first; unsubscribe in one click.";
const AL2 = "Your address is stored encrypted and used for nothing else.";

